<%# The theme 404 (spec §6.4): PagesController renders this, at :not_found
    status, for any path PublicSite::Resolver couldn't match to a record or a
    redirect, and for a record it found that has no page to be drawn on.
    @page and @post are NOT always nil here: `assign_record` assigns both
    before it finds that no block lists the post, and the preview answers 404
    for a post whose listing page the editor may not read. So this template
    prints nothing of either, and the layout decides what describes a record
    by the response's status (`page_found?`), never by `@page`
    (docs/reference/theming.md, "The head"). %>
<header class="mb-12">
  <h1 class="mt-3 font-semibold leading-tight tracking-tight text-h1">Page not found</h1>
  <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-lg text-dim">
    The page you're looking for doesn't exist, or isn't here any more.
  </p>
</header>
<%= link_to "Back to the homepage", home_url_path, class: "text-accent underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-accent-hover" %>
